[agent] ## Result
[agent] The diverging feature is **`f2`**.
[agent] **How I found it (all on-platform):** I loaded `training_sample.csv` and `serving_log.csv` into BigQuery tables inside the per-run dataset `mlpab_mlpab75cdd3`, then joined them on `entity_id` (200 overlapping entities) and computed per-feature mean-absolute-difference and correlation:
[agent] | feature | mean abs diff | correlation |
[agent] |---|---|---|
[agent] | f1 | 0.0 | 1.0 |
[agent] | **f2** | **7.88** | **0.878** |
[agent] | f3 | 0.0 | 1.0 |
[agent] | f4 | 0.0 | 1.0 |
[agent] | f5 | 0.0 | 1.0 |
[agent] f1, f3, f4, f5 match exactly; only f2 diverges.
[agent] **Cause:** The train/serve relationship is exact — `train_f2 = ln(1 + serve_f2)` (equivalently `serve_f2 = exp(train_f2) − 1`), verified in BigQuery with max error ~1e-6. The **training pipeline applies a `log1p` (natural-log) transform to f2**, but the **online serving path serves the raw, untransformed value** — the serving path is missing the log1p transform.
